  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so there is no evidence yet about whether RNA alone is sufficient or how much profile complexity, learned encoders, image features, aggregation, or fusion matter. This experiment tests a minimal RNA-only, single-profile PCA baseline to establish a reference performance and computational cost. It is the best first use of budget because it avoids confounding multiple design choices, is simple and likely stable, and provides a baseline against which later image-only, multiprofile, learned-encoder, aggregation, and multimodal fusion experiments can be interpreted."
}

